### NexusCore ###
# Build transcripts captured for milestone evidence blocks live outside the repo.
*.log
build-*.log
# Local dedicated servers used to verify each packaged JAR on the real loader.
# One per loader, named to match the project directories.
neoforgeserver/
fabricserver/
forgeserver/

# Server logs, in any loader's run directory.
*.log.gz
logs/

# The root checksums file describes the CURRENT build, so it cannot be a tracked
# record — owner ruling 2026-07-29. Committed, it was frozen at a commit while the
# jars it names changed on every build, so it drifted permanently and by design: it
# went stale twice on 2026-07-29 alone, each time within minutes of a build, and
# both times the file was *correct when written*. A record and its subject must be
# pinned to the same thing; this one could not be.
# Regenerate locally with tools/regen-checksums.sh when you want it.
# NOTE what still guarantees released bytes, because this is NOT that: the archived
# release checksums below, verified by verify-release-jar.sh and by studio-control's
# build/jar.*.sha256 — archived-vs-archived, frozen on both sides.
/checksums.txt

# Released artifacts ARE tracked on purpose: archived/ is the record of what shipped.
!archived/
!archived/**
